To turn this mock-up into a colorful and interactive website, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. First, create a basic HTML structure with a container for the joke and a button to reveal the punchline. Then, use CSS to style the container and button, and add colors and animations as desired.

For JavaScript, you can create a function to handle the button click event and reveal the punchline. You can also use JavaScript to store the punchline in a variable and update it with a new joke each time the button is clicked.

Here's a simple example of what the HTML and JavaScript might look like:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>My Joke Website</title>
  <style>
    .joke-container {
      background-color: #f2f2f2;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 10px;
    }

    .joke-button {
      background-color: #4CAF50;
      color: white;
      padding: 10px 20px;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 10px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .reveal-punchline {
      display: none;
    }

    .reveal-punchline::after {
      content: "";
      display: block;
      clear: both;
    }

    .reveal-punchline {
      animation: reveal 0.5s ease-in-out;
    }

    @keyframes reveal {
      from {
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
      to {
        transform: translateY(-10px);
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="joke-container">
    <button class="joke-button">Push to reveal punchline?</button>
    <div class="reveal-punchline">
      <p>Click the button to reveal the punchline!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    let punchline = "Click the button to reveal the punchline!";

    function revealPunchline() {
      const revealPunchline = document.querySelector(".reveal-punchline");
      revealPunchline.classList.remove("reveal-punchline");
      revealPunchline.classList.add("reveal-punchline");
    }

    const button = document.querySelector(".joke-button");
    button.addEventListener("click", revealPunchline);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```
This example uses basic CSS and JavaScript to create a simple joke website with a button to reveal the punchline. You can further enhance the website by adding animations, colors, and other interactive elements.
